Day 58 /100 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 701 - (Insert into a Binary Search Tree.)
- Problem: 701. Insert into a Binary Search Tree

- Approach:
The key is to use the BST property:
If val is greater than the current node, move to the right subtree.
If val is smaller, move to the left subtree.
Continue until an empty (null) position is found.
Insert the new node at that position.
I used an iterative approach with a pointer curr to traverse the tree.
This avoids unnecessary traversal and keeps the insertion straightforward.

-Time Complexity:
O(H)- where H is the height of the BST.
-Space ComplexityO(1)- only a few pointers are used, with no recursion or extra data structures.
- Key Takeaways
1) Strengthened my understanding of Binary Search Trees
2) Learned how the BST property simplifies insertion
3) Practiced an iterative tree traversal
